{"name":"Flurries","hex":"#f2ede3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flurries","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of flurry"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of flurry"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flurries"}],"entries":[{"title":"Snow flurry","blocks":[{"text":"A snow flurry is a light snowfall that results in little or no snow accumulation. The US National Weather Service defines snow flurries as intermittent light snow that produces no measurable precipitation. In contrast, bursts of snowfall that do result in measurable snow accumulation are called snow showers. Environment Canada uses a different definition for flurries, approximately equivalent to 'snow shower'."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/20080307_Niagara_Square_to_Lafayette_Square.JPG/330px-20080307_Niagara_Square_to_Lafayette_Square.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow_flurry","wikidata":"Q2247306"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Strawberry on white background","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Strawberry_on_white_background.jpg/500px-Strawberry_on_white_background.jpg","ratio":1.618,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Strawberry_on_white_background.jpg","share":0.704375},{"title":"Piece of chocolate cake on a white plate decorated with chocolate sauce","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Piece_of_chocolate_cake_on_a_white_plate_decorated_with_chocolate_sauce.jpg/500px-Piece_of_chocolate_cake_on_a_white_plate_decorated_with_chocolate_sauce.jpg","ratio":1.4699946893255444,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piece_of_chocolate_cake_on_a_white_plate_decorated_with_chocolate_sauce.jpg","share":0.505625},{"title":"Snow flurries in April - geograph.org.uk - 3401055","image":"https://thumb.